config BR2_PACKAGE_OPTEE_KEY
	bool "optee-key"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_OPTEE_CLIENT
	help
	  Command line tool for a device key held in OP-TEE's PKCS #11
	  token: initialise the token, generate an EC P-256 keypair
	  inside the secure world, read back the public key, and sign
	  with the private one.

	  The private key is generated as a sensitive, non-extractable
	  token object, so it never leaves the trusted application.

	  A separate process rather than a library binding, because
	  Cryptoki is initialised here for single-threaded use and the
	  whole exchange with the TA happens on one thread.

comment "optee-key needs optee-client"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_OPTEE_CLIENT
